/**
\page lua_api_sound Sound

\tableofcontents

You can create, play, or pause sound effects through \c sol.sound.

\section lua_api_sound_functions Functions of sol.sound

\subsection lua_api_sound_create sol.sound.create(sound_id, [language_specific])

Creates a sound effect.

This creates an OGG Vorbis (<tt>.ogg</tt>) formatted sound effect.

Generates a Lua error if the sound does not exist.

- \c sound_id (string): Name of the sound file to create.
- \c language_specific (boolean, optional): Check whether or not 
  if the sound is created based on the language version. 

\section lua_api_sound_methods Methods of sol.sound

\subsection lua_api_sound_play sound:play()

Plays the created sound effect.

This method does not play if a sound was not previously created.

\subsection lua_api_sound_stop sound:stop()

Stops the created sound effect.

\subsection lua_api_sound_is_paused sound:is_paused()

Checks whether the created sound is paused during playback.

- Return value (boolean): \c true if the sound is paused, \c false if it is
  not paused.

\subsection lua_api_sound_set_paused sound:set_paused([paused])

Pauses the sound effect if it is currently playing.

- \c paused (boolean, optional): \c true to pause the sound, \c false to
  unpause it. No value means \c true.

*/